%[text] %[text:anchor:TMP_3e1f] ## Glossary
%[text] %[text:anchor:M_2e0e] The **Superposition Principle**  in electromagnetism states that the total electric field created by multiple sources is the vector sum of the fields produced by each source individually. It allows straightforward calculation of complex field interactions.
